WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.810
Lamp for reps. Part six: your numbers.

2
00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:08.480
Dashboard shows your numbers only. Admins see the whole team.

3
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:15.730
Pick the period: seven days, thirty days, this month, last month, year to date, or all time.

4
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:21.050
The north star is merchants funded. It's the one number that matters.

5
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.230
Under it: dollars funded, commission expected, and commission received.

6
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:32.040
Start to money counts how many files reached each step this period. Find where yours stall.

7
00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:38.560
How long it takes shows the typical days from file to funders, to first offer, to funded.

8
00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:44.480
Pipeline right now counts your open files by stage. Click a stage to see its files.

9
00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:50.880
Stuck lists files with no movement in three days or more. Clear it every day.

10
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.510
Money shows your deals.

11
00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:59.640
Funded this month is what your deals brought in. Deals on the books counts your merchants still paying.

12
00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:09.610
Clawback watch lists deals funded in the last thirty days. If the merchant defaults that early, the funder can take the commission back. Call them.

13
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:17.790
Renewal radar watches deals as they're paid down. From about half paid, the merchant can usually renew. That's your best call.

14
00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:22.270
Call. Note. Move the stage. Fund the deal.
